1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,489
At the Corner Cafe, new staff ask Asha the
same questions every week.

2
00:00:05,509 --> 00:00:07,014
How much is a scone?

3
00:00:07,034 --> 00:00:08,538
Which cake has nuts?

4
00:00:08,558 --> 00:00:09,910
Is the soup vegan?

5
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:11,883
A wrong price is embarrassing.

6
00:00:11,903 --> 00:00:15,166
A wrong answer about nuts can make a
customer ill.

7
00:00:15,787 --> 00:00:19,047
Welcome to Chapter 20, the fourth boss
level!

8
00:00:19,067 --> 00:00:23,923
Asha will build a staff quiz from three
modules, and she will write its tests

9
00:00:23,943 --> 00:00:24,937
before its code.

10
00:00:24,967 --> 00:00:30,230
An AI assistant will write part of the
code, and promise that it passes every

11
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:30,574
test.

12
00:00:30,594 --> 00:00:32,907
The tests will have the last word.

13
00:00:33,483 --> 00:00:34,685
Here is the mission.

14
00:00:34,705 --> 00:00:37,983
A quiz with four questions about prices
and allergens.

15
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:42,303
After each answer, it says Correct, or it
gives the right answer.

16
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:45,773
At the end, a score, a percentage and a
grade.

17
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:49,176
And this time, Asha works like a software
team.

18
00:00:49,196 --> 00:00:50,694
The tests come first.

19
00:00:51,287 --> 00:00:53,545
Every piece comes from Module 4.

20
00:00:53,565 --> 00:00:55,397
Functions from Chapter 16.

21
00:00:55,433 --> 00:00:59,533
Pure functions with one job each, from
Chapter 17.

22
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:02,137
Your own modules, from Chapter 18.

23
00:01:02,167 --> 00:01:04,537
And pytest from Chapter 19.

24
00:01:04,567 --> 00:01:06,650
Plus one new pytest option.

25
00:01:06,670 --> 00:01:13,114
Dash dash t b equals no hides the details
of each failure, so the report is a short

26
00:01:13,134 --> 00:01:13,504
list.

27
00:01:14,083 --> 00:01:17,286
The quiz has three files, each with one
job.

28
00:01:17,306 --> 00:01:19,483
Quiz data holds the questions.

29
00:01:19,533 --> 00:01:21,753
Quiz logic holds the rules.

30
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,110
Quiz app does the talking: it asks and
prints.

31
00:01:25,133 --> 00:01:27,286
And a test file checks the rules.

32
00:01:27,887 --> 00:01:29,709
Here is one finished run.

33
00:01:29,729 --> 00:01:32,437
A new barista answers four questions.

34
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:34,985
The soup is vegan, so no was wrong.

35
00:01:35,005 --> 00:01:37,307
The quiz gives the right answer.

36
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:41,303
Three out of four is 75 percent: the grade
Ready.

37
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:44,021
The app itself is only fourteen lines.

38
00:01:44,041 --> 00:01:46,229
The rules live in another file.

39
00:01:46,817 --> 00:01:49,737
Asha writes down what done means.

40
00:01:49,767 --> 00:01:50,419
One and two.

41
00:01:50,439 --> 00:01:53,727
The questions live in one module, and the
rules in another.

42
00:01:53,747 --> 00:01:55,017
No rule asks or prints.

43
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:55,461
Three.

44
00:01:55,481 --> 00:01:59,807
Spaces and capitals do not matter, and a
blank answer is wrong.

45
00:01:59,833 --> 00:02:00,697
Four and five.

46
00:02:00,717 --> 00:02:04,863
A whole-number percentage, a grade, and a
last line like this one.

47
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:05,458
And six.

48
00:02:05,478 --> 00:02:11,022
Eight tests, written first, all pass, and
four typed runs give known results.

49
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:13,613
Quick check, from Chapter 17.

50
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:16,805
Why must the check answer rule not call
input?

51
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:28,302
B.

52
00:02:28,322 --> 00:02:31,150
A test calls the rule with fixed values.

53
00:02:31,170 --> 00:02:35,136
A rule that waits for a person to type
cannot be tested.

54
00:02:35,753 --> 00:02:36,756
Take a breather.

55
00:02:36,776 --> 00:02:39,313
You know the files, and what done means.

56
00:02:39,333 --> 00:02:43,328
Next, Asha plans the functions with an AI
assistant.

57
00:02:48,050 --> 00:02:53,213
In this project, all six AI stages help
build one module: the rules.

58
00:02:53,233 --> 00:02:54,280
Stage 1: plan.

59
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:58,930
Asha asks for the functions she needs, and
says: no code yet.

60
00:02:58,967 --> 00:03:02,290
The AI suggests three files and four
functions.

61
00:03:02,310 --> 00:03:08,052
The first one, ask and check, asks the
question with input, checks the answer and

62
00:03:08,072 --> 00:03:09,617
returns True or False.

63
00:03:09,667 --> 00:03:12,203
Asha checks it against criterion two.

64
00:03:12,223 --> 00:03:17,176
Ask and check does two jobs, and one of
them waits for a person to type.

65
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:18,627
No test can check it.

66
00:03:18,667 --> 00:03:22,653
So she keeps the three files and the last
three functions.

67
00:03:22,673 --> 00:03:27,972
She replaces the first one with a pure
rule: check answer, given and correct.

68
00:03:27,992 --> 00:03:28,870
The app asks.

69
00:03:28,890 --> 00:03:30,459
The rule only compares.

70
00:03:31,050 --> 00:03:32,093
Time to build.

71
00:03:32,113 --> 00:03:33,384
Step 1: the data.

72
00:03:33,404 --> 00:03:38,700
Each question is a dictionary with two
keys, a question and an answer.

73
00:03:38,733 --> 00:03:42,703
The list on lines 3 to 8 keeps the four
questions in order.

74
00:03:42,733 --> 00:03:44,749
The name is in capital letters.

75
00:03:44,769 --> 00:03:49,869
Programmers use capitals for a value that
the program reads but never changes.

76
00:03:50,487 --> 00:03:55,187
This short program imports the list from
the module, as in Chapter 18.

77
00:03:55,233 --> 00:03:57,962
Line 5 takes the first dictionary.

78
00:03:57,982 --> 00:04:01,842
Lines 6 and 7 print its question and its
answer.

79
00:04:13,213 --> 00:04:14,215
4 questions.

80
00:04:14,235 --> 00:04:19,493
Then the first question, price of a tea,
and its answer, 3.50.

81
00:04:20,083 --> 00:04:21,809
Step 2 is the big change.

82
00:04:21,829 --> 00:04:24,952
Asha writes the tests before any rule
exists.

83
00:04:24,972 --> 00:04:29,003
Line 3 imports the four rules she plans to
write, by name.

84
00:04:29,033 --> 00:04:32,213
Lines 6 and 7: an exact answer is right.

85
00:04:32,233 --> 00:04:36,453
Lines 10 and 11: spaces and capitals are
still right.

86
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,695
Lines 14 to 19 use assert not.

87
00:04:38,715 --> 00:04:41,206
It checks that something is false.

88
00:04:41,226 --> 00:04:44,825
A wrong answer and a blank answer must not
count.

89
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:49,784
Lines 22 and 23: three out of four is 75.

90
00:04:49,804 --> 00:04:54,810
Lines 26 and 27: two out of three rounds
to 67.

91
00:04:54,833 --> 00:05:01,103
Lines 31 to 34 test the edges of each
grade: 75 and 74, then 50 and 49.

92
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:06,279
And line 38 tests the whole last line.

93
00:05:06,887 --> 00:05:09,786
To run the tests, the rules need names.

94
00:05:09,806 --> 00:05:13,528
Asha writes each function with only its
docstring.

95
00:05:13,548 --> 00:05:14,427
No code yet.

96
00:05:14,467 --> 00:05:19,708
A function whose body is only a docstring
returns None, as in Chapter 16.

97
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:35,899
Asha runs pytest with dash q and dash dash
t b equals no.

98
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:38,051
Two pass, and six fail.

99
00:05:38,071 --> 00:05:41,490
The six fail as expected, because there is
no code.

100
00:05:41,533 --> 00:05:42,985
Here is something new.

101
00:05:43,005 --> 00:05:46,464
If and not treat None as false, so not
None is True.

102
00:05:46,484 --> 00:05:50,813
That is why the wrong-answer and
blank-answer tests pass already.

103
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:54,400
A test that says this must be false is
weak on its own.

104
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:59,094
The exact-answer test is its partner, and
it fails until the rule works.

105
00:05:59,687 --> 00:06:00,429
Quick check.

106
00:06:00,449 --> 00:06:02,080
You write the tests first.

107
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:05,320
What should most of them do before any
code exists?

108
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:16,810
C.

109
00:06:16,830 --> 00:06:17,186
Fail.

110
00:06:17,206 --> 00:06:21,990
A test that checks real behaviour fails
until the code is right.

111
00:06:22,010 --> 00:06:24,543
That failure is the starting line.

112
00:06:25,117 --> 00:06:25,693
Step 3.

113
00:06:25,713 --> 00:06:28,677
Asha writes the first rule herself.

114
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:33,834
Line 7: strip removes the spaces around
the answer, and lower removes the

115
00:06:33,854 --> 00:06:34,469
capitals.

116
00:06:34,489 --> 00:06:38,988
The correct answer gets lower too, so the
data may use capitals.

117
00:06:50,347 --> 00:06:52,431
Asha runs the tests again.

118
00:06:53,053 --> 00:06:54,685
The four answer tests pass.

119
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:57,683
The first four characters of the report
are dots.

120
00:06:57,733 --> 00:07:00,695
The four rules without code still fail.

121
00:07:00,715 --> 00:07:04,135
One step at a time, the dots replace the
F's.

122
00:07:04,753 --> 00:07:05,792
Stage 2: write.

123
00:07:05,812 --> 00:07:07,627
Asha wrote her rule first.

124
00:07:07,647 --> 00:07:12,003
Now she asks the AI for its own version,
without showing hers.

125
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:14,412
The AI calls lower before strip.

126
00:07:14,432 --> 00:07:15,761
A different order.

127
00:07:15,781 --> 00:07:20,708
Asha renames it ai version, so both
functions can sit in one file.

128
00:07:20,728 --> 00:07:22,357
Does the order matter?

129
00:07:22,953 --> 00:07:26,030
Asha runs both on the same four answers.

130
00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:28,043
Line 10 holds the answers.

131
00:07:28,067 --> 00:07:33,536
Exclamation mark r in line 11 prints each
answer with its quotation marks, so you

132
00:07:33,556 --> 00:07:36,247
can see the spaces and the empty answer.

133
00:07:36,267 --> 00:07:39,817
Every row matches: True, True, False,
False.

134
00:07:39,837 --> 00:07:43,225
Both versions agree, so she keeps her own.

135
00:07:43,820 --> 00:07:44,467
Breather.

136
00:07:44,487 --> 00:07:46,022
Relax your shoulders.

137
00:07:46,042 --> 00:07:48,910
One rule is done, and the tests say so.

138
00:07:48,933 --> 00:07:52,635
Next, Asha lets the AI write the other
three rules.

139
00:07:57,383 --> 00:07:57,883
Step 4.

140
00:07:57,903 --> 00:07:59,220
Stage 3: generate.

141
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:03,455
Asha pastes her tests and asks for the
other three rules.

142
00:08:03,475 --> 00:08:05,163
Do not change my tests.

143
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:10,021
The AI writes the module, and says: this
passes all eight of your tests.

144
00:08:10,041 --> 00:08:11,030
It sounds sure.

145
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:12,176
Look at line 12.

146
00:08:12,196 --> 00:08:17,609
Remember floor division from Chapter 2:
the double slash keeps only the whole

147
00:08:17,629 --> 00:08:17,962
part.

148
00:08:29,313 --> 00:08:29,475
0.

149
00:08:29,495 --> 00:08:34,639
Three double slash four is 0, and 0 times
100 is still 0.

150
00:08:34,659 --> 00:08:36,995
The AI's promise is wrong.

151
00:08:37,015 --> 00:08:39,803
Asha runs the tests to be sure.

152
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:41,527
Stage 4: test.

153
00:08:41,547 --> 00:08:45,149
Asha runs her eight tests on the AI's
module.

154
00:08:45,169 --> 00:08:48,128
The first four dots are her own rule.

155
00:08:48,148 --> 00:08:50,060
Then F, F, a dot, and F.

156
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:54,713
Three tests fail: three of four,
percentage rounds, and result line.

157
00:08:55,320 --> 00:09:00,694
She asks the AI what the three failing
tests have in common, and says: do not fix

158
00:09:00,714 --> 00:09:01,560
anything yet.

159
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,519
All three call percentage.

160
00:09:03,539 --> 00:09:07,992
Two test it directly, and result line uses
it for the score.

161
00:09:08,587 --> 00:09:09,695
Stage 5: debug.

162
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:15,638
Asha copies one failing test into a small
file of its own, and runs it with the

163
00:09:15,658 --> 00:09:20,227
details on, using dash dash t b equals
short from Chapter 19.

164
00:09:20,267 --> 00:09:25,373
The report shows the test line, and the
real value: 0, not 75.

165
00:09:25,393 --> 00:09:30,168
The where line says the 0 came from
percentage of 3 and 4.

166
00:09:30,787 --> 00:09:35,657
She pastes the report and asks for the
cause first, then the smallest fix.

167
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:38,250
The AI explains the double slash.

168
00:09:38,270 --> 00:09:43,311
Its fix divides with a single slash first,
and rounds at the end.

169
00:09:43,331 --> 00:09:44,635
One line changes.

170
00:09:45,253 --> 00:09:48,109
Asha does not run only the test that
failed.

171
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:49,743
She runs all eight again.

172
00:09:49,767 --> 00:09:50,559
Eight dots.

173
00:09:50,579 --> 00:09:51,519
Eight passed.

174
00:09:51,539 --> 00:09:54,103
The AI sounded sure the first time.

175
00:09:54,123 --> 00:09:57,056
The tests were the only thing that knew.

176
00:09:57,653 --> 00:09:58,427
Quick check.

177
00:09:58,447 --> 00:09:59,552
You fix one rule.

178
00:09:59,572 --> 00:10:01,405
Which tests do you run next?

179
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:12,900
D.

180
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:13,741
All of them.

181
00:10:13,761 --> 00:10:18,435
A small fix can break something else, and
only a full run shows it.

182
00:10:19,053 --> 00:10:19,616
Breather.

183
00:10:19,636 --> 00:10:22,593
The rules are finished, and every test
passes.

184
00:10:22,633 --> 00:10:24,898
Now, the app that does the talking.

185
00:10:29,650 --> 00:10:30,193
Step 5.

186
00:10:30,213 --> 00:10:33,730
Lines 3 and 4 import the data and two
rules.

187
00:10:33,767 --> 00:10:36,447
The loop on line 7 takes each question.

188
00:10:36,467 --> 00:10:37,485
Line 8 asks it.

189
00:10:37,505 --> 00:10:40,947
Plus a space puts a space after the
question mark.

190
00:10:40,967 --> 00:10:45,917
Lines 9 to 11: if the rule says right,
print Correct, and add a point.

191
00:10:45,967 --> 00:10:49,927
Otherwise, lines 12 and 13 give the right
answer.

192
00:10:49,967 --> 00:10:54,398
Line 14 hands the count to result line and
prints what it returns.

193
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:55,730
Your turn.

194
00:10:55,750 --> 00:10:58,797
A new barista gets all four answers right.

195
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:13,525
Score, 4 out of 4, 100 percent, Ready.

196
00:11:14,117 --> 00:11:15,866
The rules pass their tests.

197
00:11:15,886 --> 00:11:17,767
Now Asha tests the whole app.

198
00:11:17,787 --> 00:11:23,206
Each run is a copy of the app with its own
typed answers, and a last line she knows

199
00:11:23,226 --> 00:11:23,927
in advance.

200
00:11:23,967 --> 00:11:26,017
Full marks, which you predicted.

201
00:11:26,067 --> 00:11:26,453
Zero.

202
00:11:26,473 --> 00:11:32,957
Three for the tea is close to 3.50, but it
is not the same text, so it is wrong.

203
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,630
Spaces and capitals.

204
00:11:34,667 --> 00:11:36,349
And four blank answers.

205
00:11:36,953 --> 00:11:38,889
The spaces and capitals run.

206
00:11:38,909 --> 00:11:44,058
For the cake, the barista types CARROT in
capitals, with spaces around it.

207
00:11:55,413 --> 00:11:55,713
Yes.

208
00:11:55,733 --> 00:12:00,267
Strip removes the spaces, and lower
removes the capitals.

209
00:12:00,287 --> 00:12:00,906
Correct!

210
00:12:00,926 --> 00:12:03,143
All four count: 100 percent.

211
00:12:03,163 --> 00:12:03,542
Pass.

212
00:12:04,153 --> 00:12:05,591
Four blank answers.

213
00:12:05,611 --> 00:12:10,117
Each one gets the right answer printed,
and the score is 0.

214
00:12:10,137 --> 00:12:10,808
No crash.

215
00:12:10,828 --> 00:12:11,191
Pass.

216
00:12:11,787 --> 00:12:13,228
Here are the results.

217
00:12:13,248 --> 00:12:16,567
Every real last line matches what Asha
expected.

218
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:19,988
All four runs pass, and so do the eight
tests.

219
00:12:20,583 --> 00:12:21,878
Stage 6: improve.

220
00:12:21,898 --> 00:12:23,269
Every test passes.

221
00:12:23,289 --> 00:12:29,453
Asha asks the AI to make grade shorter,
and says: do not change what it returns.

222
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:34,968
The AI says: drop elif and else, because
return already stops the function.

223
00:12:34,988 --> 00:12:36,505
That idea is correct.

224
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:39,830
Here is the AI's shorter version.

225
00:12:39,850 --> 00:12:46,199
Read line 17 carefully, and compare it
with Asha's rule: 75 or more is Ready.

226
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:58,196
Almost.

227
00:12:58,216 --> 00:13:03,288
Line 17 says greater than 75, not greater
than or equal.

228
00:13:03,308 --> 00:13:05,470
The AI changed one sign.

229
00:13:06,087 --> 00:13:07,543
Asha runs her tests.

230
00:13:07,563 --> 00:13:13,153
Two fail: the grade boundaries, and the
last line, which now ends in Almost,

231
00:13:13,173 --> 00:13:14,777
because it uses grade.

232
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:20,193
Line 31, the boundary test from step 2,
found it in less than a second.

233
00:13:20,787 --> 00:13:25,250
Asha keeps her own grade, and runs all
eight tests one more time.

234
00:13:25,270 --> 00:13:26,147
Eight passed.

235
00:13:26,753 --> 00:13:30,143
Here are all six stages, on one module of
rules.

236
00:13:30,167 --> 00:13:34,507
The AI helped at every stage, from the
plan to the improvement.

237
00:13:34,533 --> 00:13:39,960
And it was confidently wrong three times:
the plan, the percentage, and the shorter

238
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:40,353
grade.

239
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:45,981
Every time, something Asha wrote first
caught it: criterion two, then her tests.

240
00:13:46,587 --> 00:13:47,426
Last breather.

241
00:13:47,446 --> 00:13:50,987
You built software with tests, and you
made the decisions.

242
00:13:51,033 --> 00:13:52,086
Let's recap.

243
00:13:56,817 --> 00:13:59,127
Here is what you used in this boss level.

244
00:13:59,167 --> 00:14:03,437
Split a program by job: data, rules, and
the app that talks.

245
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:09,297
Keep rules pure, with no input and no
print, so a test can check them.

246
00:14:09,333 --> 00:14:10,850
Write the tests first.

247
00:14:10,870 --> 00:14:13,853
With no code yet, most of them should
fail.

248
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:15,084
Give an AI your tests.

249
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,343
Then run them yourself.

250
00:14:16,363 --> 00:14:18,047
The report decides, not the AI.

251
00:14:18,067 --> 00:14:21,285
And test the edges, such as exactly 75.

252
00:14:21,887 --> 00:14:23,851
One last check, on an edge.

253
00:14:23,871 --> 00:14:27,819
With Asha's final rules, what does grade
of 50 return?

254
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:39,344
A.

255
00:14:39,364 --> 00:14:39,989
Almost.

256
00:14:40,009 --> 00:14:43,948
50 is not 75 or more, but it is 50 or
more.

257
00:14:43,968 --> 00:14:47,907
An edge, and the test on line 33 checks
it.

258
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:50,048
Boss level complete!

259
00:14:50,068 --> 00:14:53,841
You earned 300 XP and the Software Builder
badge.

260
00:14:53,861 --> 00:14:55,467
And Module 4 is done.

261
00:14:57,587 --> 00:15:02,107
The practice file has eight more tasks,
worth 170 XP.

262
00:15:02,133 --> 00:15:07,103
Three warm-ups, worth 10 XP each, such as
checks before you trust a rule.

263
00:15:07,133 --> 00:15:11,760
Three apply tasks, worth 20 each,
including tests first for the change a

264
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:12,663
customer gets.

265
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:15,221
And two stretch tasks, worth 40 each.

266
00:15:15,241 --> 00:15:19,960
In the last one, you fix an AI's counter
that skips the first answer.

267
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,470
Write the checks first, then the code.

268
00:15:23,050 --> 00:15:25,412
The quiz works, and every test passes.

269
00:15:25,432 --> 00:15:28,483
But when the quiz closes, every score
disappears.

270
00:15:28,503 --> 00:15:30,990
Asha cannot see who needs more practice.

271
00:15:31,033 --> 00:15:36,961
In Chapter 21, you will save data to a
file and load it again, so the cafe keeps

272
00:15:36,981 --> 00:15:37,853
every score.

273
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:39,569
Do the warm-up tasks now.

274
00:15:39,589 --> 00:15:41,460
They take about ten minutes.

275
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:43,376
See you in Chapter 21.
